# CF-WO-P1-002-R1-R1: files whose raw bytes the routing catalog hashes
# must check out with LF on every platform. A Windows checkout
# converting LF to CRLF changes their SHA-256 and fails the catalog
# freshness checks (CF-P1-002-CATALOG) — PR run #237 proved it: both
# windows-compat jobs failed exactly the source-SHA-256 and
# skill-fingerprint checks. The checkout contract is pinned here,
# not in code: the fingerprint semantics are unchanged and no hash
# is ever normalised. Rebuild the catalog, never hand-edit it; see
# docs/runtime/SKILL_ROUTING_RUNTIME.md ("The catalog").
architecture/SKILL_ROUTING_MATRIX.yaml eol=lf
architecture/WORKFLOW_GRAPH.yaml eol=lf
architecture/intent-modes.yaml eol=lf
architecture/COMPANION_CAPABILITY_REGISTRY.yaml eol=lf
architecture/AGENT_COMPATIBILITY_MATRIX.yaml eol=lf
skills/*/SKILL.md eol=lf
registry/routing-catalog.json eol=lf
